    "narrative": "For this July 4th slate, **Brice Turang** (75.06) and **Corbin Carroll** (73.47) emerge as our definitive anchors. **Brice Turang** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Kelly, and his leadoff spot provides the high-volume opportunities we prioritize in 5x5 formats. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential start; despite a middling matchup against Woodruff, the 100% stolen base efficiency rating against the pitcher\u2019s delivery cycle creates a high ceiling for both counting stats and our scarcest category, SB. **Josh Naylor** rounds out our elite tier at 70.49, capitalizing on a juicy matchup against Bieber, where his platoon advantage and favorable SP projections heavily outweigh the minor park penalty.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Cole Young**. His 48.12 projection put him within striking distance of the final utility slots, but he ultimately lost out to the superior lineup position of **Alex Freeland** and the efficiency metrics of **Austin Riley**. While **Cole Young** benefits from the same SP skill boost as **Josh Naylor**, his slotting in the #7 hole significantly suppresses his run-production potential relative to our starters. We are also keeping a close watch on **James Wood** (51.23); his elite 0.418 xwOBA is currently being hampered by an elite-level SP matchup against Ashcraft, making him a \"start on talent\" play rather than a \"start on matchup\" play today.\n\nRegarding roster risks, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Dalton Rushing** (46.97) and **Alex Freeland** (49.35). Both are facing Peralta, whose 4.54 xERA is exploitable, but their low position in the batting order limits their efficiency scores. We have opted to start them to conserve game caps while maintaining a respectable floor. Please note that **Trevor Story** remains on the IL and is unavailable for consideration, and we have confirmed that **Jose Caballero** is absent from today's lineup entirely, reinforcing the importance of our current configuration to maximize our daily Roto output.",
